\check Report of Figure captions v1.1
\submenu Phil_new
\script Find_caption.py
\description Scans selected books for \fig figure markers, lists each figure's caption, copyright text, and illustration file name directly in the results list (one row per item; "empty" or "Copyright: empty" when missing), and writes a FigureCaptions.html report (opened automatically) listing every figure's reference, caption, copyright, and illustration file. When the project's figures folder has a picture for a figure (the same name, or a .jpg copy of a .tif), a "Show picture thumbnails" checkbox at the top of the report shows a small copy of each picture. Each figure is automatically classified as USFM 2 (pipe-delimited fields) or USFM 3 (key="value" attributes) based on its content, so no version needs to be selected. If a FigureCaptionsDebug.log appears in the project folder, something unexpected happened -- please share it. [Version 1.1]
\books
\noText
\toList
\utf8

\optionName DisplayCaption
\optionLocalizedName Display caption?
\optionDescription Yes includes a Caption column in the report and a results-list row with the caption text (or "empty") for every figure.
\optionDefault Yes

\optionName DisplayCopyright
\optionLocalizedName Display copyright?
\optionDescription Yes includes a Copyright column in the report and a results-list row with the copyright text (or "Copyright: empty") for every figure.
\optionDefault Yes

\optionName DisplayIllustrationFile
\optionLocalizedName Display illustration file name?
\optionDescription Yes includes an Illustration File column in the report and a results-list row with the illustration's file name (e.g. "CN01629B.TIF" or "MyrrhBush_HK00118.tif") for every figure, or "empty" if none is specified. For USFM 3 this is the src="..." attribute; for USFM 2 it is the field right after the first pipe.
\optionDefault Yes

\optionName SortByCaption
\optionLocalizedName Sort captions alphabetically
\optionDescription Yes sorts the figures listed in the HTML report alphabetically by the figure's caption text, so identical or near-identical captions end up next to each other for easy comparison. If captions are hidden (Display caption = No), sorts by the illustration file name instead (if shown); if both are hidden, sorts by copyright text instead. No (default) lists them in canonical book/chapter/verse scan order. Accented/diacritic characters are ignored when determining sort order (but are still displayed normally).
\optionDefault No
